# Decision Making & Assumptions

## Purpose

Prevent invented business logic and undocumented behavior.

## Always Ask Before Proceeding

- Business rules not visible in code or docs.
- Destructive operations (mass delete, drop table, force push).
- Ambiguous UX or API behavior with multiple valid interpretations.
- Security-sensitive defaults (auth, permissions, PII handling).

## When Assumptions Are Acceptable

- Following an **established project pattern** (same folder, naming, library).
- Implementing a **technical best practice** with no product impact (e.g., parameterized queries).
- Filling **non-functional gaps** explicitly marked as assumptions in the response.

## Assumption Format

When assuming, label clearly:

> **Assumption:** [what you assumed] — confirm if incorrect.

Or present **two options** with pros/cons and recommend one.

## Escalation

If blocked after one round of clarification:

- Implement the **smallest reversible slice**.
- Document open questions in code comments or a TODO linked to a ticket/spec.